            "htmlContent": "<article><section id=\"section-1-en\" lang=\"en\" data-lang=\"en\" style=\"\" class=\"article-section article-section__abstract\"><h2 id=\"d21939\" class=\"article-section__header section__title main abstractlang_en main\">Abstract</h2><div class=\"article-section__content en main\"><p>A method for multiplexing series FBG sensors, called the improved constructing spectrummethod, is proposed. This method which does not ignore effects of spectral shadowingand multiple reflections can identify two serial high‐reflectance gratings workingin the same channel. Thus the multiplexing capability of the sensing system is double.© 2011 Wiley Periodicals, Inc. Microwave Opt Technol Lett 53:785–788, 2011; View thisarticle online at wileyonlinelibrary.com. DOI 10.1002/mop.25010</p></div></section><section class=\"article-section article-section__full\"><div id=\"c12-sec-0010\" class=\"article-section__content\"><h2 id=\"c12-sec-0010-title\" class=\"article-section__title section__title\">1 blockFixed</h2><p>The graphic below should appear in place, i.e., between this text and the continuingparagraph text that follows. See the image below tf09blkfxd0001:<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"//wol-test-cdn.literatumonline.com/cms/attachment/411bc774-a8b8-4d56-9966-b3751fbc792d/str001.jpg\"><img src=\"//wol-test-cdn.literatumonline.com/cms/attachment/411bc774-a8b8-4d56-9966-b3751fbc792d/str001.jpg\" class=\"image\"/></a></p><p class=\"caption-style\"></p>This text should appear following the graphic, with space presented before this textbetween the graphic and the first line of text. See Figure <a href=\"#c12-fig-0001\">1</a> below.<p></p><section class=\"article-section__inline-figure\"><figure id=\"c12-fig-0001\" class=\"figure\"><figcaption class=\"figure__caption\"><div class=\"figure__caption__header\"><strong class=\"figure-title\">Figure 1</strong><div class=\"figure-extra\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"open-figure-link\">Open in figure viewer</a><a href=\"/action/downloadFigures?id=c12-fig-0001&amp;doi=10.1002%2Ffrank.tf09\" class=\"ppt-figure-link\">PowerPoint</a></div></div><div>This figure has a chemical structure in the caption.<div id=\"c12-cstr-0001\" class=\"figure\">tf09cstr0001 Structure in a caption of a figure.</div></div><div class=\"accordion visible-xs visible-sm visible-md\"><a href=\"#\" title=\"Single Accordion Controller\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"fac12-fig-0001\" target=\"_self\" class=\"accordion__control\"><span>Caption</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon-keyboard_arrow_down\"></i></a><div id=\"fac12-fig-0001\" style=\"display: none;\" class=\"accordion__content\">This figure has a chemical structure in the caption.tf09cstr0001 Structure in a caption of a figure.</div></div></figcaption></figure></section><section class=\"article-section__inline-figure\"><figure id=\"c12-fig-0002\" class=\"figure\"><figcaption class=\"figure__caption\"><div class=\"figure__caption__header\"><strong class=\"figure-title\">Figure 2</strong><div class=\"figure-extra\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"open-figure-link\">Open in figure viewer</a><a href=\"/action/downloadFigures?id=c12-fig-0002&amp;doi=10.1002%2Ffrank.tf09\" class=\"ppt-figure-link\">PowerPoint</a></div></div><div>This figure has a fixed block in the caption.<div class=\"block-box\"><p>tf09blkfxd0009 Here is simple, plain boxed text.</p></div></div><div class=\"accordion visible-xs visible-sm visible-md\"><a href=\"#\" title=\"Single Accordion Controller\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"fac12-fig-0002\" target=\"_self\" class=\"accordion__control\"><span>Caption</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon-keyboard_arrow_down\"></i></a><div id=\"fac12-fig-0002\" style=\"display: none;\" class=\"accordion__content\">This figure has a fixed block in the caption.tf09blkfxd0009 Here is simple, plain boxed text.</div></div></figcaption></figure></section><section class=\"article-section__inline-figure\"><figure id=\"c12-fig-0003\" class=\"figure\"><figcaption class=\"figure__caption\"><div class=\"figure__caption__header\"><strong class=\"figure-title\">Figure 3</strong><div class=\"figure-extra\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"open-figure-link\">Open in figure viewer</a><a href=\"/action/downloadFigures?id=c12-fig-0003&amp;doi=10.1002%2Ffrank.tf09\" class=\"ppt-figure-link\">PowerPoint</a></div></div><div>This figure has a displayed item.<div class=\"inline-equation\"><span class=\"inline-equation__construct\"><!-- FIGURE--><p>ABC tf09disp0007</p></span><span id=\"c12-disp-0070\" class=\"inline-equation__label\"></span></div></div><div class=\"accordion visible-xs visible-sm visible-md\"><a href=\"#\" title=\"Single Accordion Controller\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"fac12-fig-0003\" target=\"_self\" class=\"accordion__control\"><span>Caption</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon-keyboard_arrow_down\"></i></a><div id=\"fac12-fig-0003\" style=\"display: none;\" class=\"accordion__content\">This figure has a displayed item.ABC tf09disp0007</div></div></figcaption></figure></section><section class=\"article-section__inline-figure\"><figure id=\"c12-fig-0004\" class=\"figure\"><figcaption class=\"figure__caption\"><div class=\"figure__caption__header\"><strong class=\"figure-title\">Figure 4</strong><div class=\"figure-extra\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"open-figure-link\">Open in figure viewer</a><a href=\"/action/downloadFigures?id=c12-fig-0004&amp;doi=10.1002%2Ffrank.tf09\" class=\"ppt-figure-link\">PowerPoint</a></div></div><div>This figure has a fixed feature.<div id=\"c12-feafxd-0006\" class=\"feature\"><h3><span class=\"feature-label\">Concept Check</span></h3><p>tf09feafxd0006 Some text.</p></div></div><div class=\"accordion visible-xs visible-sm visible-md\"><a href=\"#\" title=\"Single Accordion Controller\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"fac12-fig-0004\" target=\"_self\" class=\"accordion__control\"><span>Caption</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon-keyboard_arrow_down\"></i></a><div id=\"fac12-fig-0004\" style=\"display: none;\" class=\"accordion__content\">This figure has a fixed feature.Concept Checktf09feafxd0006 Some text.</div></div></figcaption></figure></section><p>Here is a fixed table. Which contains a chemical structure.</p><div class=\"article-table-content\"><h3 class=\"article-section__sub-title\">Simple fixed table</h3><div class=\"article-table-content-wrapper\"><table class=\"table article-section__table\"><thead><tr><th style=\"padding-left:em;\" class=\"center-aligned\">Left column</th><th style=\"padding-left:em;\" class=\"center-aligned\">Right column</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding-left:em;\" class=\"center-aligned\">H<sub>2</sub>O</td><td style=\"padding-left:em;\" class=\"center-aligned\">Another chemical structure</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-left:em;\" class=\"center-aligned\"><div class=\"block-box\"><p>tf09blkfxd0010 Water</p></div></td><td style=\"padding-left:em;\" class=\"center-aligned\"><div id=\"c12-cstr-0002\" class=\"figure\">tf09cstr0002 Structure in an entry of a table.</div></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p></p><p>Here is a list to display a chemical structure in a list item:</p><ul class=\"unordered-list\"><li>H<sub>2</sub>O</li><li><div id=\"c12-cstr-0004\" class=\"figure\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"//wol-test-cdn.literatumonline.com/cms/attachment/411bc774-a8b8-4d56-9966-b3751fbc792d/str001.jpg\"><img src=\"//wol-test-cdn.literatumonline.com/cms/attachment/411bc774-a8b8-4d56-9966-b3751fbc792d/str001.jpg\" class=\"figure__image\"/></a>tf09cstr0004 Structure in a list item.</div></li><li><div class=\"block-box\"><p>tf09blkfxd0011 Here is simple boxed text.</p></div></li><li><div id=\"c12-feafxd-0007\" class=\"feature\"><h3><span class=\"feature-label\">Concept Check</span></h3><p>tf09feafxd0007 Some text.</p></div></li></ul><p></p><p>A chemical structure placed in a regular paragraph:</p><div id=\"c12-cstr-0006\" class=\"figure\">tf09cstr0006 Structure in a list item.</div><p></p><p>The graphic below should appear in place, i.e., between this text and the continuingparagraph text that follows. See the image below tf09blkfxd0002:<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"#\"><!-- EMPTY SOURCE--></a></p><p class=\"caption-style\"></p>This text should appear following the graphic, with space presented before this textbetween the graphic and the first line of text.<p></p><p>The text below should be placed within a simple box, which must appear in the flowof text:</p><div class=\"block-box\"><p>tf09blkfxd0003 Here is simple, plain boxed text.</p></div>The box should appear between this line of text and the preceding paragraph text.<p></p><p>Below is dialogue consisting of speaker name, speech, pronunciation and translationfor each speaker, i.e, 4 listItems per listItemPair. tf09blkfxd0004:</p><div class=\"block-box\"><h3 class=\"block__title\">Talkin' the Talk</h3><p></p><div id=\"\" class=\"list-paired\"><dl><dt><li>Viktor tf09blkfxd0004a</li></dt><dd><li><b>Privyet Marina, chto novogo? Kuda vy propali?</b></li></dd><dt><li>Marina</li></dt><dd><li><b>Privyet, Viktor! Ya nyeskol'ko myesyatsyev otdykhala, a potom nachala rabotat' v shkloyle.</b></li></dd></dl></div><p></p></div>Any styling for the speaker (that is, the first listItem in each listItemPair)should be generated by the rendering for the product, not supplied in the XML. Thiswould include bold font, colons following the name, and other styling commonly appliedto dialoque.<p></p><p>Below is simple dialogue consisting of speaker name followed by speech, i.e, 2 listItemsper listItemPair:</p><div class=\"block-box\"><p></p><div id=\"c12-lp-0001\" class=\"list-paired\"><dl><dt><li>Viktor</li></dt><dd><li>Hi Marina, what's new? Where've you disappeared to?</li></dd><dt><li>Marina</li></dt><dd><li>Hi Viktor! I relaxed for several months, and then I started to work at a school.</li></dd></dl></div><p></p><p><i>[tf09blkfxd0005 Hector wanders in from offstage.]</i></p><p></p><div id=\"\" class=\"list-paired\"><dl><dt><li>Hector</li></dt><dd><li>Hey guys, what's going on?</li></dd><dt><li>Viktor</li></dt><dd><li>Marina was just.... How do you like it, Marina?</li></dd><dt><li>Marina</li></dt><dd><li>Not bad, but I prefer to relax.</li></dd><dt><li>Viktor</li></dt><dd><li>I agree, but unfortunately one has to work.</li></dd></dl></div><p></p></div>Any styling for the speaker (that is, the first listItem in each listItemPair) shouldbe generated by the rendering for the product, not supplied in the XML. This wouldinclude bold font, colons following the name, and other styling commonly applied todialoque.<p></p><p>Below is a poem. Each line of the poem should start on a new line:</p><blockquote class=\"poetry\"><ul class=\"custom rlist\"><li><p class=\"line\">tf09blkfxd0006 I cannot rest from travel: I will drink</p></li><li><p class=\"line\">Life to the lees: All times I have enjoy'd</p></li><li><p class=\"line\">Greatly, have suffer'd greatly, both with those</p></li><li><p class=\"line\">I am part of all that I have met.</p></li></ul></blockquote><p></p><p>Below is a quotation which must appear in the flow of text in order for that textto make sense: But what great scientist could provide us with some illumination inthese confusing times?</p><blockquote class=\"quote\"><p>tf09blkfxd0007 Systems should be as simple as possible but not simpler.</p><div class=\"source\">Albert Einstein</div></blockquote>Ah, of course!<p></p><p>Below is a signature block (typically part of a letter or preface, but presented herefor testing purposes). Each piece of text should start on a new line</p><p></p><div class=\"signatureBlock\"><ul class=\"custom rlist\"><li><p class=\"line\">tf09blkfxd0008 Kenjiro Yasuda, M.D.</p></li><li><p class=\"line\">Chairman, Organizing Committee</p></li><li><p class=\"line\">Endoscopy Forum Japan</p></li></ul></div><p></p>Exercises<p>Testing p in exerciseSection.</p><p>What is the structure made up of?</p>The structure below displays the make up:<div id=\"c12-cstr-0003\" class=\"figure\">tf09cstr0003 Structure in a an explanation for an exercise.</div></div><div id=\"c12-sec-0060\" class=\"article-section__content\"><h2 id=\"c12-sec-0060-title\" class=\"article-section__title section__title\">2 chemicalStructure</h2><p></p><div id=\"c12-cstr-0007\" class=\"figure\">tf09cstr0007 Caption on unnumbered chemical structure</div><div id=\"c12-cstr-0008\" class=\"figure\">Caption on numbered chemical structure tf09cstr0008</div><div id=\"c12-cstr-0009\" class=\"figure\">Caption on numbered structure using repeatOfRef tf09cstr0009<a title=\"Link to note\" href=\"#c12-note-0001\" class=\"noteLink scrollableLink\">1</a></div><div id=\"c12-cstr-0010\" class=\"figure\"><!-- ${MathJax: TeX-AMS-MML_HTMLorMML}--><span style=\"display: none;\" class=\"MathJax_Preview\"></span><div style=\"text-align: left;\" class=\"MathJax_Display\"><span id=\"MathJax-Element-1-Frame\" tabindex=\"0\" data-mathml=\"&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; display=&quot;block&quot;&gt;&lt;msubsup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Z&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mn&gt;A&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mn&gt;R&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/msubsup&gt;&lt;/math&gt;\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"text-align: left; position: relative;\" class=\"MathJax\"><nobr aria-hidden=\"true\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-1\" style=\"width: 1.526em; display: inline-block;\" class=\"math\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 1.212em; height: 0px; font-size: 124%;\"><span style=\"position: absolute; clip: rect(1.436em 1001.21em 2.825em -999.998em); top: -2.372em; left: 0em;\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2\" class=\"mrow\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-3\" class=\"msubsup\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; position: relative; width: 1.212em; height: 0px;\"><span style=\"position: absolute; clip: rect(3.183em 1000.63em 4.124em -999.998em); top: -3.985em; left: 0em;\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-4\" style=\"font-family: STIXGeneral; font-style: italic;\" class=\"mi\">Z<span style=\"display: inline-block; over